 "notes": "F = k_pair * 2 r_c * (theta_c - theta), finger.md 6.2 linear model. theta_c is the T09 first-contact angle (same samples); the floor is absolute, so the uncalibrated spread of theta_c moves the force at the floor. Reading used: the servo position errors at contact and at the floor are independent (deadband and gear play settle afresh at each stop), so the floor error has its own sample key (shared: servo_angle_error_at_floor) and T09's contact error stays inside theta_c. With one common bias instead (contact error cancelled explicitly) the stack is still FAIL (third review, B1: Cpk 0.95 against 0.90 here); the shared T09 key used before cancelled the floor error sample for sample and made the stack read MARGINAL.",
